Cell["The three symmetry types", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7305c70e-705e-a349-a2b3-70f7e78999a4"],

Cell["\<\
The symmetry type of each edge is visible in the drawing. A directed edge \
carries arrowheads running along it, from its first vertex to its last. An \
unordered edge carries none. A cyclic edge carries none either, and is marked \
instead by a small circular arrow at its centre:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3f86757f-a49e-1e46-acb2-bf63f44a1541"],

Cell["\<\
Grid[{
   {\"Directed\", \"Unordered\", \"Cyclic\"},
   HypergraphPlot[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2, 3, 4}, #]}], ImageSize -> 170] & /@
     {\"Directed\", \"Unordered\", \"Cyclic\"}
  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Center]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c78778e1-fa42-0645-9d9b-d5332d1c09bd"],

