Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "The badge is drawn with Offset, so its radius is a fixed number of \
printer's points rather than a fraction of the embedding. A plot-relative \
radius looked right on one example and wrong on the next, because the extent \
of a spring embedding has nothing to do with how big the label text is."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"3e3ed100-55c0-d94f-aa11-eb4ec269591d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "Vertex labels are shown by default: a vertex's label when it has one, and \
otherwise its identifier. The reference paclet shows nothing by default. Here \
the identifier is the thing that makes a vertex what it is, and reading \
identifiers off the picture is what makes the isomorphism examples below \
checkable by eye, so it seemed the more useful default. VertexLabels -> None \
turns them off."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"a6a72f1f-d02c-594b-bca5-7b8d018f8915"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "The colours are the reference's light-mode colours, on an explicit white \
background. The reference wraps each colour in LightDarkSwitched on 14.3 and \
later, but that wrapper is only resolved by a live front end; rendered from a \
plain kernel it is an unrecognized directive and the entire plot comes out as \
an error box. A fixed palette renders identically everywhere."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"0a1ceaf2-a386-2945-9a39-a62d40e054b7"],

Cell["Displaying as a Graph does", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"65c71543-6174-7044-bb67-e1cf7d890233"],

Cell["\<\
The picture is not merely a picture of the hypergraph: it is the hypergraph. \
Feeding the displayed output back to the kernel recovers the object, exactly \
as it does for a Graph:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68ca210b-c087-7544-873d-33165c982abe"],

Cell["\<\
ToExpression[ToBoxes[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}]]] === Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, \
{2, 3}}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f5f5c490-e75b-644a-88db-2afdbb4c5c56"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"7989e960-5686-ba41-aff4-db85a1af40b0"],

Cell["\<\
A hypergraph too large to draw usefully falls back to a summary box instead, \
with the thresholds adjustable through SetHypergraphPlotThresholds:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0011912c-8af7-d64c-b53a-2073ce80000f"],

Cell["Hypergraph[Table[Edge[{i, i + 1}], {i, 40}]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a51d5498-ba4b-c149-ad5a-dae7344ca1ae"],

