Cell["\<\
A directed edge is never the same as an unordered one, so a and au are not \
isomorphic:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"875cb016-b0f5-bd44-95cb-c840a79c027c"],

Cell["IsomorphicHypergraphQ[a, au]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"70813dc2-17f7-cb48-8349-c60fe8d384d1"],

Cell[BoxData["False"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"35450b6a-10a7-554e-94b2-39c82a1a9fb0"],

Cell["Labels count only up to renaming", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"558ce71c-e0d0-3d4d-add4-f21731f306d0"],

Cell["\<\
The two hypergraphs below are the same directed path, one carrying edge \
labels a and b, the other x and y. They are isomorphic: on top of the vertex \
renaming sits the label correspondence a \[Rule] x, b \[Rule] y.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fbffaf1a-072f-0e42-b52c-677532e225d1"],

Cell["\<\
h1 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"a\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Directed\", \"b\"]}];
h2 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"y\"]}];
{h1, h2}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5829176f-835d-f14a-9b51-b9e4204cf8ee"],

