Cell["\<\
h3 below is the same path again, but carries the one label x on both of its \
edges. It is not isomorphic to h1, because a correspondence would have to \
send both a and b to x, and that is not one-to-one. What distinguishes the \
two is not the names of the labels but how many edges share each of them:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c8ac3889-41a2-f44c-a10b-fd5187669152"],

Cell["\<\
h3 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"x\"]}];
{h1, h3}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9ca9437e-b1f5-7248-b483-381754c76459"],

