Cell["\<\
l1 and l2 are both the labelled path A \[Rule] B \[Rule] C, so they are \
isomorphic. So, now, is l3, the path C \[Rule] B \[Rule] A: leaving the \
vertices where they are and exchanging the labels A and C carries one to the \
other, and exchanging two labels is a perfectly good one-to-one \
correspondence:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f7077a80-3ac2-7c41-bc29-937dcd0f586e"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[l1, l2],
  IsomorphicHypergraphQ[l1, l3],
  IsomorphicHypergraphQ[l1, l3, \"Labeled\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c3bba320-629a-3643-9666-f549979b7b8b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->\
"9504d83a-2dcb-164f-a8f9-a50b9c0a41f7"],

Cell["FindHypergraphIsomorphism[l1, l2]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f20e8a3d-6454-5b40-9db6-2ccc12c7616a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"1", "\[Rule]", "10"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[Rule]", "20"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "30"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",Expres\
sionUUID->"2e61b9a6-3eff-9f49-871c-beab6a7f0fc4"],

Cell["\<\
What a renaming cannot repair is a difference in how the labels are shared \
out. Two labellings of the same path, one reading A, A, B and the other A, B, \
B, are still not isomorphic: any correspondence would have to send A to both \
A and B at once. Their skeletons of course agree. This is also the case the \
upstream paclet gets wrong:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04b8a345-d081-2a49-acfb-f6253b230344"],

Cell["\<\
m1 = Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"A\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}];
m2 = Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}];
{m1, m2}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"80c684b5-0aed-d64e-ab7a-41ba032f3a7b"],

