Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Design note.  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "An edge's label sits alongside its symmetry type in its identity, so the \
isomorphism search never treats labels as a separate pass. The canonical form \
replaces each label by a placeholder numbered from the structure, after which \
two edges match when the Edge expressions match, which settles vertex labels, \
edge labels, symmetry and multiplicity in one comparison."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameMargins->{{10, 0}, {6, 6}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.7],
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.25],ExpressionUUID->"f42e0dae-7aed-8e4c-bf07-cb74c9c5603a"],

Cell["Skeletons", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f842886a-b4e6-754b-9025-5c7eaeaab870"],

Cell["\<\
The skeleton \[LongDash] the underlying unlabelled hypergraph, with all \
symmetry types kept \[LongDash] is available on its own. The labels A, B, C \
give way to the bare identifiers:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"067aa64d-2478-da42-a29d-5c19d2e6a391"],

Cell["{l1, HypergraphSkeleton[l1]}", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0c4b11cc-17de-c14d-aeb6-8d028caac12c"],

