Cell["CanonicalHypergraph[a] === CanonicalHypergraph[b]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bb05a177-1148-354a-9fcc-aa27fc0747b9"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"bbfc7f14-a560-3447-8e67-48d5a4c35a6a"],

Cell["\<\
In the labelled case the labels do not travel with their vertices, because \
their values are not part of what is being canonicalized. They are replaced \
by placeholders \[FormalL][1], \[FormalL][2], \[Ellipsis] numbered from the \
structure, which is exactly what makes two hypergraphs differing only by a \
renaming of labels come out identical. Dropping the labels altogether gives \
the canonical form of the skeleton:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6c787cb0-53b7-094c-bf87-4c9fc4e1fa5a"],

